        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:14 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: BRUCE E. JOHNSON, ESQ., Des Moines, Iowa; on behalf of the Petitioners. EDMUND J. SEASE, ESQ., Des Moines, Iowa; on behalf of the Respondent. LAWRENCE G. WALLACE, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, in support of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bruce E. Johnson",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The patents in this case that have been issued on plant varieties under section 101 of title 35 are invalid. They're invalid because Congress has enacted a specific statutory scheme that it crafted to govern Federal statutory protection over this particular type of living thing, plant varieties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: The rights conferred by the statute you're referring to are somewhat different than the patent statute, aren't they?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bruce E. Johnson",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Every -- all 17 corn plant varieties that are the subjects of the patents that we have challenged in this case also applied for and obtained Plant Variety Protection certificates."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edmund J. Sease",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It was not the intent of Congress to inject itself into marketing situations that are governed by State law or by the Federal Seed Act. It had one thing in mind and that was to regulate the right to exclude others from sexually multiplying plant varieties. It wasn't in the market of suing people who just bought the bagged seed, didn't do anything with it, sold it to farmers who just planted that seed and took it to the elevator."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edmund J. Sease",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The PVP requires that you give the breeding history. There's no requirement of that for the patent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I take it that's your position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edmund J. Sease",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SEASE: That's an infringement of the utility patent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Edmund J. Sease",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SEASE: He can pay for permission. That's correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sease",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But one of the reasons why utility patent protection is so critically important to people in this industry is because that seeds are so easily copied by self-replicating. And so, if you can qualify for the higher standard, you need to have that higher standard because of the ease of replication."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lawrence G. Wallace",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Diamond against Chakrabarty, the Plant Patent Act and the Plant Variety Protection Act played a central role in the debates between counsel and between the Court's opinion and the dissenting opinions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Wallace, can I ask you your view on the question of whether a person who buys a patented seed and plants it and then gets some seeds and saves them and then replants them the following year, would he be an infringer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1996",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a6f14db4cf364d5a31e7011feea2ff1d5627a46e5729cb0ddcec1c5da7d63219",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a6f14db4cf36-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
